// @error no field 'hidden' on Box
// D1191 — AN UN-EXPORTED `self`-FUNCTION IS NOT CALLABLE FROM ANOTHER MODULE.
// `hidden` is declared in `./lib`, never exported, and used there via UFCS. The
// merge's plain-name alias table answered THIS call with lib's mangled function,
// so `b.hidden()` compiled and printed 42 — while the direct spelling `hidden(b)`
// was `undeclared identifier 'hidden'` in the same file. UFCS now resolves against
// the CALLER's scope, which is the direct call's rule.
//
// The diagnostic is the plain one: `ufcs-not-imported` (D1230) offers only an
// EXPORTED function, and there is no import that would make this call resolve.
import { mk } from "./lib"

const b = mk(21)
print(b.hidden())
